<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>NYT &gt; Technology</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/section/technology</link><description>Technology industry news, commentary, and analysis, with reporting on big tech, startups, and internet culture. The New York Times is a hub for conversation about news and ideas.</description><atom:link rel="self" href="https://rss.nytimes.com/services/xml/rss/nyt/Technology.xml" type="application/rss+xml" /><item><title>Meta Launches New Facebook Marketplace App Called Seller</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/24/technology/meta-facebook-marketplace-seller.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/24/technology/meta-facebook-marketplace-seller.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</guid><atom:link rel="standout" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/24/technology/meta-facebook-marketplace-seller.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss" /><description>Seller is part of the Silicon Valley company’s strategy to innovate on its original social network.</description><dc:creator>Eli Tan</dc:creator><pubDate>Fri, 24 Jul 2026 11:00:09 GMT</pubDate><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Meta</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Facebook</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Mobile Apps</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">E Commerce</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Online advertising</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Social Media</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Computers and the Internet</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Tech Industry</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Customer service</category><media:content url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/07/24/multimedia/24biz-facebook-marketplace-1-flpt/24biz-facebook-marketplace-1-flpt-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600.jpg" medium="image"><media:credit>Ian C. Bates for The New York Times</media:credit><media:description>The Menlo Park, Calif., headquarters of Meta, which introduced a stand-alone app for Facebook Marketplace sellers on Friday. </media:description></media:content></item><item><title>How Meta’s Threads Became as Popular as X</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/05/technology/threads-meta-twitter-x.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/05/technology/threads-meta-twitter-x.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</guid><atom:link rel="standout" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/05/technology/threads-meta-twitter-x.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss" /><description>The social platform that Meta once positioned as a rival to Elon Musk’s X now has 500 million monthly users. It increasingly resembles Reddit.</description><dc:creator>Eli Tan</dc:creator><pubDate>Sun, 05 Jul 2026 09:01:42 GMT</pubDate><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Meta</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Social Media</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Threads</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Artificial intelligence</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Instagram</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Facebook</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Mark E Zuckerberg</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">X</category><media:content url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/06/30/multimedia/META-THREADS-1-03-tgph/META-THREADS-1-03-tgph-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600.jpg" medium="image"><media:credit>Ian C. Bates for The New York Times</media:credit><media:description>“We want to be the largest and best platform for public conversation,” said Connor Hayes, the head of Threads. </media:description></media:content></item><item><title>Judge Extends Pause for Paramount-Warner Bros. Deal</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/23/technology/judge-paramount-warner-bros-deal.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/23/technology/judge-paramount-warner-bros-deal.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</guid><atom:link rel="standout" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/23/technology/judge-paramount-warner-bros-deal.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss" /><description>The court blocked the companies from closing the acquisition through mid-August, as a judge considers two lawsuits challenging it.</description><dc:creator>David McCabe</dc:creator><pubDate>Thu, 23 Jul 2026 23:34:45 GMT</pubDate><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Warner Bros. Discovery</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Paramount Skydance</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Mergers and Acquisitions</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Competition law</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Lawsuits</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Federal Courts</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Decisions and Verdicts</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Movies</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">TV</category><media:content url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/07/23/multimedia/23biz-paramount-1-bflz/23biz-paramount-1-bflz-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600.jpg" medium="image"><media:credit>Ricardo Nagaoka for The New York Times</media:credit><media:description>The Paramount lot in Los Angeles.</media:description></media:content></item><item><title>OpenAI Models Go Rogue + Kimi K3 Freakout + A.I. Superforecasting</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/24/podcasts/hardfork-hugging-face-openai.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/24/podcasts/hardfork-hugging-face-openai.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</guid><atom:link rel="standout" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/24/podcasts/hardfork-hugging-face-openai.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss" /><description>“The story that we’re talking about in this segment was science fiction until Tuesday, OK?”</description><dc:creator>Kevin Roose, Casey Newton, Whitney Jones, Rachel Cohn, Davis Land, John Woo, Alyssa Moxley, Dan Powell, Elisheba Ittoop, Marion Lozano and Leah Shaw Dameron</dc:creator><pubDate>Fri, 24 Jul 2026 11:00:03 GMT</pubDate><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">science</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">OpenAI</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Hugging Face</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Artificial intelligence</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">internal-open-access-audio</category><media:content url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/07/24/podcasts/24hardfork-openai-hug/24hardfork-openai-hug-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600.png" medium="image"><media:credit>The New York Times</media:credit></media:content></item></channel></rss>